  "title": "Kirby Problem 1.55",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Suppose that $C$ is a ribbon concordance from a fibered knot $K_{1}$\nto a fibered knot $K_{0}$.\n(a) Does the capped-off monodromy of $K_{1}$ (i.e. extended over a disk) extend to\na compression body whose lower boundary gives the capped-off monodromy\nof $K_{0}$?\n(b) Is $C$ fibered by compression bodies?\n(c) Suppose a fibered knot in a homology 3-sphere bounds a homotopy-ribbon\ndisk $D$ in a contractible 4-manifold $V$ . Is $V \\setminus\\nu(D)$ fibered by handlebodies?",
